      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Extraction of Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Aqua Regia is a freshly prepared 3:1 mixture of concentrated Hydrochloric Acid (HCl) and concentrated Nitric Acid (HNO3), capable of dissolving Gold and Platinum.",
        "Sodium and Potassium are stored under kerosene oil to prevent violent reactions with atmospheric oxygen and moisture.",
        "Amphoteric oxides like Aluminium Oxide (Al2O3) and Zinc Oxide (ZnO) react with both acids and bases to yield salt and water.",
        "Cinnabar (HgS) is the primary ore of mercury, which is converted to mercuric oxide (HgO) and reduced to mercury upon heating in air."
      ],
      "id": "iers7jh"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9f4xwhq",
      "content": "• Highly reactive metals are extracted by electrolysis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gigfl0a",
      "content": "• Moderately reactive metals are extracted by reduction using carbon."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cei7cuz",
      "content": "• Less reactive metals are often found in free state."
    },
    {
      "id": "4g3w9vv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hsm5umg",
      "content": "• Metals are good conductors of heat and electricity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c8uwuw0",
      "content": "• Non-metals are generally poor conductors."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zcq4qsp",
      "content": "• Mercury is the only metal that is liquid at room temperature."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g68oupx",
      "content": "• Gold and silver are least reactive metals."
    }
